        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;To fulfill all righteousness&#x27;: Cyril stresses the anamartetos Word needs no baptism for sin — he submits to John&#x27;s baptism to sanctify the waters themselves for our regeneration. The Tewahedo Tǝmqät mass riverside baptism, repeated annually with congregational immersion, descends directly from this Cyrillian rationale of water-sanctification.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
