        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Till heaven and earth pass, one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s iota-keraia Torah-immutability text. The incarnate Word does not abrogate but confirms; even the smallest stroke of Torah is fulfilled in Christ. Tewahedo OT-and-NT equally-canonical practice rests on this Cyrillian Torah-respect.</p></aside>',
