        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Be ye therefore perfect as your heavenly Father is perfect&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s classic theosis-summons. The divine perfection is the trajectory, not the achievement; God-likeness is the Spirit&#x27;s ongoing transforming work in the saints. Tewahedo Andǝmta locates teleiōsis (perfection) in the Spirit&#x27;s continual conformation, never in moral mastery.</p></aside>',
