        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Thy kingdom come; thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven&#x27; — Cyril treats the two petitions as inseparable. The basileia-coming IS the will-done; Pentecost begins what Parousia completes. Tewahedo eschatology preserves the inaugurated-and-awaited tension precisely this way in the Mäzämmǝr-of-the-kingdom.</p></aside>',
