        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Give us this day our daily bread&#x27; — Cyril is the locus classicus on epiousios. He glosses the term as &#x27;super-substantial&#x27; — the bread that is above ordinary substance, the Eucharistic-and-providential bread together. Tewahedo Qǝddāse explicitly cites Mt 6:11 (with the epiousios Greek term retained in the Geʿez exegesis) at the fraction-rite.</p></aside>',
