        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors&#x27; — Cyril names this the only conditional petition; the disciple voluntarily ties God&#x27;s mercy to his own. The hōs (as) is not metric (forgive-by-same-measure) but causal (the forgiving heart receives because it can receive). Tewahedo Lord&#x27;s-Prayer preaching foregrounds this hōs heavily.</p></aside>',
