        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;First cast out the beam out of thine own eye&#x27; — Cyril reads the dokos-karphos hyperbole (beam-mote) as exposing self-blindness; the corrector who has not first repented cannot see clearly enough to help. Tewahedo spiritual-direction tradition takes Mt 7:5 as the qualifying-examination for any abba.</p></aside>',
