        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Himself took our infirmities, and bare our sicknesses&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s Isa 53 christological-fulfillment locus. Matthew explicitly cites Isa 53:4; Cyril reads the healings of Matt 8 as proleptic Passion-fulfillment — the Suffering Servant absorbs human weakness here in the Galilean ministry already, prefiguring the Cross. Tewahedo Mäshafä-Mistir reads Mt 8:17 as the hermeneutical key: every Gospel healing is a partial Cross-event; the Cross is the universal healing.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
