        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves: be ye therefore wise as serpents, and harmless as doves&#x27; — Cyril marks the phronimoi-akeraioi (wise-harmless) pairing as complementary, not contradictory. Serpent-wisdom is diagnostic acuteness about danger; dove-harmlessness is non-aggression in response. The Cross-Spirit synthesis: neither naive nor predatory. Tewahedo monastic-pastoral discernment tradition cites Mt 10:16 as the abba&#x27;s-balance text.</p></aside>',
