        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And ye shall be hated of all men for my name&#x27;s sake: but he that endureth to the end shall be saved&#x27; — Cyril reads hypomeinas eis telos as the martyric perseverance-summary. The dia to onoma mou (for my name&#x27;s sake) is the specifically-Christic hatred; persecution as such is not blessed (per Mt 5:10). The end (telos) is teleological-eschatological — through-to-the-end, not until-it-stops. Tewahedo Sämā&#x27;ǝtāt martyrology cites Mt 10:22 as the perseverance-charter.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
