        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;The Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath&#x27;: Cyril reads this not as Sabbath-abrogation but as Sabbath-fulfillment in the person of Christ who is himself the Rest toward which the Sabbath always pointed. Tewahedo&#x27;s distinctive dual-Sabbath observance (Saturday Sänbäte-Ayhud + Sunday Sänbäte-Krǝstiyan) traces theologically to this Cyrillian dual-fulfillment.</p></aside>',
