        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother&#x27; — Cyril reads the redefined-family text carefully — not as displacement of Mary (who emphatically DOES the Father&#x27;s will, the supreme fiat-mihi of Lk 1:38) but as expansion-of-kinship via obedience. Tewahedo Marian-theology reads Mt 12:50 as doubly-affirming Mary: she is mother-by-flesh AND mother-by-obedience, the latter being the criterion she singularly meets.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
