        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The parable of wheat and tares: Cyril cautions strongly against premature ecclesial purgation. The mixed-Church is the present economy; the eschatological judgment alone separates without error. Tewahedo monastic-discernment traditions cite this parable against perfectionist schism.</p></aside>',
