        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God&#x27;: Cyril treats Peter&#x27;s confession as the Christological summit of the Synoptic narrative — the apostolic shorthand of the homoousion. Tewahedo Anaphora preserves this confession verbatim in the pre-Communion dialogue between celebrant and people.</p></aside>',
