        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;If any man would come after me, let him deny himself and take up his cross and follow me&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s discipleship-charter. The cross is not metaphor but anticipated participation in the Lord&#x27;s passion. Tewahedo monastic and martyric vocations are read as the two modes of cross-carrying — daily mortification and witness-unto-death.</p></aside>',
